// Title: RestrictedAdminMode Registry Value Tampering - ProcCreation
// Sigma ID: 28ac00d6-22d9-4a3c-927f-bbd770104573
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2023-01-13 | Modified: 2025-08-28
// ATT&CK: persistence, defense-impairment, T1112
// Description: Detects changes to the "DisableRestrictedAdmin" registry value in order to disable or enable
//   RestrictedAdmin mode. RestrictedAdmin mode prevents the transmission of reusable credentials to
//   the remote system to which you connect using Remote Desktop. This prevents your credentials from
//   being harvested during the initial connection process if the remote server has been compromise
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/a8e3cf63e97b973a25903d3df9fd55da6252e564/atomics/T1112/T1112.md
//   - https://social.technet.microsoft.com/wiki/contents/articles/32905.remote-desktop-services-enable-restricted-admin-mode.aspx
//   - https://thedfirreport.com/2022/05/09/seo-poisoning-a-gootloader-story/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_reg_lsa_disable_restricted_admin.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa" and ProcessCommandLine contains "DisableRestrictedAdmin"
